# Default: every text file normalizes to LF on every platform.
# Byte-pinned artifacts below opt out with -text.
* text=auto eol=lf

# sha-bearing artifacts: bytes are load-bearing (manifest_sha256 in receipts,
# shard sha256 chains). git must NEVER rewrite line endings at checkout.
corpus-manifests/** -text
receipts/** -text
tokenizer/** -text
# R3 board-canonicality (fspec-R3-1436): this exact file is an additive,
# byte-identical copy of the -text-pinned receipts/ember-totality-
# 20260711T103912Z.json (C-FED evidence). Its own directory has no -text
# pin, so without this line the default `* text=auto eol=lf` above would
# silently normalize its CRLF bytes on add/checkout, breaking the D1
# byte-identical twin-adjudication this copy exists to satisfy. Same class
# as the receipts/** pin above -- same reason, narrower scope.
scripts/ember_totality/receipts-totality/ember-totality-20260711T103912Z.json -text
# docs/research/ holds raw-byte-pinned premises (fp26_prereg pins the decision
# artifact's sha256 over exact on-disk bytes); CRLF normalization on Windows
# checkouts drifts those bytes and fails the prereg premise. Pin -text (eng-47).
